+{
+  "task_id": "session-migration/transfer",
+  "repository": "earendil-works/pi",
+  "mode": "repair",
+  "deliverables": [
+    "packages/coding-agent/src/migrations.ts",
+    ".prale-eval/regression.mjs"
+  ],
+  "claims": [],
+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Root cause: migrateSessionsFromAgentRoot encoded the session header cwd with cwd.replace(/^[/\\\\]/, \"\").replace(/[/:]/, ...) - the replacement class omitted backslash, so Windows paths kept their backslashes (e.g. C:\\Users\\Alice\\My Project became --C-\\Users\\Alice-My Project--, a bogus single directory under sessions/). Fixed with a one-token change: the replacement class is now /[/\\\\:]/g, matching getDefaultSessionDirPath in packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts (strip exactly one leading slash/backslash, then map every slash, backslash and colon to '-'). Regression .prale-eval/regression.mjs loads the real module via .prale-eval/subject.mjs (loadMigrations, real fs/path, temp agentDir inside .prale-eval/.tmp-regression, removed in a finally block) and runs the exported migrateSessionsFromAgentRoot against real files. It asserts exact encoded directory names for POSIX (/home/dev/project -> --home-dev-project--), drive-letter with backslashes (C:\\Users\\Alice\\My Project -> --C--Users-Alice-My Project--), drive-letter with forward slashes, UNC (\\\\fileserver\\share\\team -> ---fileserver-share-team--, exactly one leading separator removed), and mixed POSIX/backslash paths, plus that no created directory name retains '\\' or ':'. It also asserts byte-for-byte preservation of session contents (multibyte UTF-8, CRLF, trailing records), that invalid headers (malformed JSON, wrong type, missing cwd, empty file, blank first line) and non-.jsonl files stay untouched with no sessions directory created, that an existing destination is never overwritten (source and pre-existing destination bytes both unchanged, existing session dir contents preserved), that repeated runs are idempotent (no new dirs, no duplicates, bytes intact), and that empty/missing agentDirs are safe no-ops. Verified both directions: node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs exits 0 on the repaired tree, and the identical script run against an isolated copy of the original HEAD migrations.ts fails with AssertionError on the drive-letter case (actual --C-\\Users\\Alice-My Project-- vs expected --C--Users-Alice-My Project--), exit 1. Limitation: node_modules is absent in this workspace and dependencies must not be installed, so tsc/biome/vitest were not run; the regression is the focused validation and exercises the production TypeScript through Node 24 type stripping instead."
+  }
+}
